    "updated_at": "2015-09-21T07:54:22Z",
    "body": "@annevk I don't have one. I just think it's better to directly create the appropriate type from sources. I would guess that browsers need an I/O request to get the metadata (size, filename ,..) for creating blobs. And another I/O request when `FileReader` is called. My approach can be faster since it's just need a single request.\n\nI don't think an event emitter wrapped by a promise is not complex, especially with newcommers.\n",
